se not but basically quantum  superman is grant morrison's adaptation  of dr manhattan which is an interesting  concept considering that dr manhattan  was actually inspired  by captain adam but we also learned from  the little bit of information that we're  given that quantum superman is one of  the most powerful beings  in the entire multiverse and because of  this immense power  he's scared of what he has become and  takes drugs to curb his quantum senses  which is a form of near omniscience that  grants him knowledge unbound by time  or space now being under the influence  of these power dampening drugs  makes it possible for adam to be largely  controlled by his bosses in the military  which would not be possible  if you are tapping into quantum senses  quantum superman the only superpowered  being on his earth  goes on to join a team known as pax  americana designed to maintain peace and  order in the united states  along with peacemaker blue beetle the  question and nightshade and so this is  basically the watchmen if the original  plan  of using charlton characters instead of  original characters had actually come to  fruition and so moving on to his powers  quantum superman is virtually omniscient  and omnipotent he's remarked that he  observes the three-dimensional world  in much the same way that we observe the  two-dimensional worlds of comic books he  was also able to interface  with the ultimate thule's computer a  piece of monitor technology  and was able to process 100 yota bytes  of  information in seconds i have no idea  what unibytes are but it sounds like a  lot adam is also able to create multiple  copies of himself  much in the same way that dr manhattan  was able to do so and he can also alter  the size of himself  as well as his copies his most  impressive power however is his ability  to alter reality which he claims to be  able to do in eight dimensions  and while we don't see many examples of  this due to the limited number of  appearances 